        "title": "Cloud App Control versus URL Filtering: which applies"
      },
      {
        "rel": "see-also",
        "to": "zia.ssl-inspection.pipeline",
        "title": "Where SSL inspection sits in ZIA web policy evaluation (the two passes)"
      }
    ],
    "checks": [
      {
        "do": "Which category the URL belongs to, since it is resolved before any rule is walked.",
        "uses": [
          "zia.url-categories.membership:resolved-before-rules"
        ]
      },
      {
        "do": "Whether a higher rule fails to fire only because the URL resolved to a different category.",
        "uses": [
          "zia.url-categories.membership:resolved-before-rules",
          "zia.url-filtering.rule-order:ascending-order"
        ]
      },
      {
        "do": "Whether a disabled rule is the reason a higher rule appears not to fire.",
        "uses": [
          "zia.url-filtering.rule-order:disabled-holds-slot"
        ]
      },
      {
        "do": "Whether an admin rank limits the positions a rule can take in the order.",
        "uses": [
          "zia.url-filtering.rule-order:admin-rank-precedes"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "prose": {
      "text": "URL Filtering is a first-match policy. URL Filtering rules evaluate in ascending `order` (Rule 1 before Rule 2). [ascending-order] Evaluation stops at the first rule whose criteria all match; later rules are not consulted. [first-match]\n\n**Category first.** Which category a URL is in is decided before any rule is walked: [Category membership is resolved before rules are walked: a rule matches a URL through the category the URL resolved to, not through every category with a matching entry.](kb:zia.url-categories.membership:resolved-before-rules).\n\n**Disabled rules and admin ranks.** A disabled rule is skipped but keeps its position in the order. [disabled-holds-slot] With Admin Rank enabled, a rule's admin rank (0 is highest, 7 lowest) constrains the order values it can take: a higher-ranked rule always precedes a lower-ranked one, and an admin cannot pick a rank above their own. [admin-rank-precedes]\n\n**Rules that never run.** If Cloud App Control explicitly allows the transaction, URL Filtering does not run unless cascading is enabled ([Cloud App Control versus URL Filtering: which applies](kb:zia.cloud-app-control.precedence)). On inspected HTTPS, URL Filtering runs twice, once on the domain and once on the full URL ([Where SSL inspection sits in ZIA web policy evaluation (the two passes)](kb:zia.ssl-inspection.pipeline)).",
      "order": [
        "ascending-order",
        "first-match",
        "disabled-holds-slot",
        "admin-rank-precedes"
      ]
    }
  },
